@OnePunchMonk I reproduced a regression in the packed-QKV change: after `fuse_qkv_projection()`, calling `block.to(dtype=torch.float64)` and then `_project_qkv()` with a float64 input fails with `mat1 and mat2 must have the same dtype`. The same probe passes on this PR's base commit. I ran the actual projection methods with small CPU Linear layers, not a full model run.

`_fused_qkv_weight` and `_fused_qkv_bias` are now plain Tensor attributes, so module device/dtype conversions do not move them, and rebinding the individual weights breaks their shared-storage relationship. The loader refresh hook does not cover those transitions. Please account for device/dtype moves and layerwise offload when rebuilding or invalidating this cache, with one focused transition test.

Could you keep this PR focused on camera precision and split the independent QKV, RoPE and sequence-parallel changes into follow-up PRs? That will make the fixes much easier to review and validate.

